research_notes.finding:
Pattern: Use @google/generative-ai/sdk package for TypeScript
Installation: pnpm add @google/generative-ai
Import: import { GoogleGenerativeAI } from '@google/generative-ai';

Initialization:
const genAI = new GoogleGenerativeAI(process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY);
const model = genAI.getGenerativeModel({ model: 'gemini-pro' });

Content Generation:
const result = await model.generateContent(prompt);
const response = await result.response;
const text = response.text();

Note: The API key should come from credential vault, not env var

Repository: mozilla/pdf.js
Pattern: pdf.getDocument().promise.then(pdf => {
  const metadata = pdf.pdfInfo;
  return {
    title: metadata.info.Title,
    author: metadata.info.Author,
    subject: metadata.info.Subject,
    keywords: metadata.info.Keywords,
    creator: metadata.info.Creator,
    producer: metadata.info.Producer,
    creationDate: metadata.info.CreationDate,
    modificationDate: metadata.info.ModDate,
  };
});
Note: Some PDFs may not have metadata, use filename as fallback

architecture_patterns.pattern:
All state mutations must go through Zustand store actions
Pattern: async action(params) → update Dexie → update Zustand state
Example:
  extractMetadata: async (sourceId: string) => {
    const source = get().sources.find(s => s.id === sourceId);
    const metadata = await extractAllMetadata(source);
    await db.sources.update(sourceId, metadata);
    set((state) => ({
      sources: state.sources.map(s => s.id === sourceId ? { ...s, ...metadata } : s)
    }));
  }

Use toast notifications for user feedback
Pattern: showErrorToast('Error message', { action: 'Retry', onAction: retryFn })
Import: import { toast } from 'sonner';

Use SkeletonLoader component for loading states
Pattern: 
Import: import { SkeletonLoader } from '@/components/ui/SkeletonLoader';

Pattern for mocking useKnowledgeStore:
vi.mock('@/lib/state/knowledge-store', () => ({
  useKnowledgeStore: vi.fn(),
}));

(useKnowledgeStore as unknown as ReturnType).mockReturnValue({
  sources: mockSources,
  extractMetadata: vi.fn(),
  updateMetadata: vi.fn(),
});

technical_notes.note:
CRITICAL: Use credential vault for API key storage
Import: import { credentialVault } from '@/lib/agent/providers/credential-vault';
Pattern: const apiKey = await credentialVault.getCredential('google-gemini');
NEVER hardcode API keys or use environment variables directly
